texts.en:
Undertakings and persons covered by this Act must apply customer due diligence procedures under sections 11 to 21 when
1) they establish a business relationship, when the relevant circumstances of a customer change and otherwise at appropriate times, including when, during the relevant calendar year, the undertaking or person is under a legal duty to contact the customer in order to review any relevant information concerning the beneficial owner or owners;
2) they carry out an occasional transaction of
a) at least EUR 15,000, whether the transaction is carried out in a single operation or in several operations that are or appear to be linked;
b) more than EUR 1,000 in the form of a transfer of funds, whether the transaction is carried out in a single operation or in several operations that are or appear to be linked;
c) EUR 500 or more in currency exchange, including exchange between crypto-assets and fiat currency, whether the transaction is carried out in a single operation or in several operations that are or appear to be linked; or
d) EUR 1,000 or more in exchange between one or more types of crypto-assets, transfers of crypto-assets or services related to the issuance of crypto-assets, whether the transaction is carried out in a single operation or in several operations that are or appear to be linked;
3) in connection with the provision of gambling services, they accept stakes, pay out winnings, or both, amounting to at least EUR 2,000, whether the transaction is carried out in a single operation or in several operations that are or appear to be linked;
4) there is a suspicion of money laundering or terrorist financing, even if the conditions in nos. 2 and 3 are not met; or
5) there is doubt as to whether previously obtained information on the customer's identity is correct or adequate.
